    "text": "Following figure shows two processes <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> for a gas. If <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> are the amount of heat absorbed by the system in two cases, and <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> are changes in internal energies, respectively, then:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0157_bc5e73d1bb90.png\" />"
